{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWJxYW8ia8E76f2nnbJ4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017aHNXijWCkjfbAWdQnPuGr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/analysis/IMPACT_REPORT.md","content":"# Impact Report: tonic → hyper → tokio Dependency Chain\n\n**Repos analyzed:** `/workspace/tokio` (tag `tokio-1.0.0`), `/workspace/hyper` (tag `v0.14.0`), `/workspace/tonic` (tag `v0.6.0`)\n\n## 1. Dependency Chain and Exact Version Constraints\n\n### tonic → hyper\n\n- `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml` (`[dependencies]`, `transport` feature):\n  ```\n  hyper = {version = \"0.14.4\", features = [\"full\"], optional = true}\n  hyper-timeout = {version = \"0.4\", optional = true}\n  h2 = {version = \"0.3\", optional = true}\n  ```\n  Pulled in when the `transport` feature is enabled (`transport = [\"h2\", \"hyper\", \"tokio\", \"tower\", ...]`, part of `default = [\"transport\", \"codegen\", \"prost\"]`).\n  Note the constraint is `0.14.4`, i.e. **strictly newer** than the `hyper` checkout in this workspace (`v0.14.0`, `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml` → `version = \"0.14.0\"`). A build against these two repos verbatim (via `path` deps) would use `0.14.0`, but a crates.io resolve of tonic 0.6.0 requires `>=0.14.4, <0.15.0` — the local checkout is below tonic's declared floor.\n- `/workspace/tonic/tonic-web/Cargo.toml`: `hyper = \"0.14\"` (direct, for its own hyper `Body`/service glue).\n- `/workspace/tonic/examples/Cargo.toml`, `/workspace/tonic/interop/Cargo.toml`, `/workspace/tonic/tests/compression/Cargo.toml`, `/workspace/tonic/tests/integration_tests/Cargo.toml` (dev-dep), `/workspace/tonic/tonic-web/tests/integration/Cargo.toml`: all pin `hyper = \"0.14\"` (or `\"0.14.3\"` in `tests/compression`).\n\n### hyper → tokio\n\n- `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml` (`[dependencies]`):\n  ```\n  tokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"sync\"] }\n  ```\n  Base requirement is always `tokio/sync` (used for `want`-adjacent oneshot/watch channels in dispatch, drain, `client::conn`, `upgrade.rs`).\n  Additional tokio features are pulled in transitively through hyper's own feature flags:\n  ```\n  runtime = [\"tcp\", \"tokio/rt\"]\n  tcp     = [\"socket2\", \"tokio/net\", \"tokio/rt\", \"tokio/time\"]\n  full    = [\"client\", \"http1\", \"http2\", \"server\", \"stream\", \"runtime\"]\n  ```\n  So `hyper` with `features = [\"full\"]` (exactly what tonic requests) transitively requires tokio features: `sync`, `net`, `rt`, `time`.\n- `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml` (`[dev-dependencies]`): `tokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"fs\",\"macros\",\"io-std\",\"io-util\",\"rt\",\"rt-multi-thread\",\"sync\",\"time\",\"test-util\"] }`, `tokio-util = \"0.6\"` — dev-only, not relevant to downstream consumers.\n\n### tonic → tokio (direct, in addition to the transitive path through hyper)\n\n- `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml`:\n  ```\n  tokio = {version = \"1.0.1\", features = [\"net\"], optional = true}\n  tokio-util = {version = \"0.6\", features = [\"codec\"]}\n  tokio-stream = \"0.1\"\n  ```\n  and the `transport` feature explicitly adds `\"tokio/macros\", \"tokio/time\"`.\n- `/workspace/tonic/tonic-health/Cargo.toml`: `tokio = {version = \"1.0\", features = [\"sync\"]}`.\n- `/workspace/tonic/tonic-reflection/Cargo.toml`: `tokio = {version = \"1.0\", features = [\"sync\"]}`, `tokio-stream = {version = \"0.1\", features = [\"net\"]}`.\n- `/workspace/tonic/tonic-web/Cargo.toml` (dev-dep): `tokio = {version = \"1\", features = [\"macros\", \"rt\"]}`.\n\n### Full chain summary\n\n```\ntonic (0.6.0)\n ├─ hyper 0.14.4  (feature \"full\")  ──┐\n │                                    ├─▶ tokio ^1  (features unify to: sync, net, rt, time, macros — via hyper's \"full\"\n ├─ tokio 1.0.1   (feature \"net\")  ───┘                and tonic's own \"tokio/macros\",\"tokio/time\" requests)\n ├─ tokio-util 0.6 (feature \"codec\")\n ├─ tokio-stream 0.1\n ├─ h2 0.3\n ├─ tower 0.4.7\n └─ tokio-rustls 0.22 (tls feature only)\n```\nChecked-out repo versions actually present: `tokio` = 1.0.0, `hyper` = 0.14.0, `tonic` = 0.6.0.\n\n## 2. tokio APIs hyper Uses That tonic Depends On Transitively\n\nhyper 0.14 has **no runtime-abstraction layer for I/O** — unlike later hyper 1.x, its `rt` module (`/workspace/hyper/src/rt.rs`) only defines the `Executor` trait; all connection I/O types are `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite}` directly. This means tokio I/O traits leak straight through hyper's public API into tonic.\n\nConcrete coupling points (grep of `tokio::` in `/workspace/hyper/src`):\n\n- **`tokio::net::TcpListener` / `tokio::net::TcpStream`** — `/workspace/hyper/src/server/tcp.rs`: `AddrIncoming` wraps a `tokio::net::TcpListener`; the inner `AddrStream` (same file, `mod addr_stream`, re-exported as `hyper::server::conn::AddrStream`) wraps a raw `tokio::net::TcpStream` and implements `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite}` on it directly (lines ~226–315).\n  - **tonic usage:** `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/conn.rs` imports `hyper::server::conn::AddrStream` and `tokio::net::TcpStream` directly to build its `Connected`/`ConnectInfo` implementations for the default server transport.\n  - `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/incoming.rs` imports `hyper::server::{accept::Accept, conn::{AddrIncoming, AddrStream}}` and bounds its generic `tcp_incoming<IO, ...>` on `IO: tokio::io::AsyncRead + tokio::io::AsyncWrite + Connected + Unpin + Send + 'static` — i.e. tonic's server transport is generic over any tokio-`AsyncRead+AsyncWrite` type, a bound inherited from hyper's `Accept`/`Server` API.\n- **`tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite, ReadBuf}`** — used pervasively in hyper's `body`, `proto::h1`, `proto::h2`, `common::io::rewind`, `upgrade.rs` to move bytes on the wire.\n  - **tonic usage:** `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/service/io.rs` defines `pub(in crate::transport) trait Io: AsyncRead + AsyncWrite + Send + 'static` (aliasing `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite, ReadBuf}`) and `BoxedIo`, tonic's type-erased connection wrapper — this is a direct re-implementation of the same tokio I/O trait bound hyper requires of its transport.\n- **`tokio::time::{Sleep, sleep, timeout, interval}`** — `/workspace/hyper/src/client/connect/http.rs` (connect timeout / happy-eyeballs fallback delay), `/workspace/hyper/src/server/tcp.rs` (accept-error backoff sleep), `/workspace/hyper/src/proto/h2/ping.rs` (HTTP/2 keepalive ping).\n  - **tonic usage:** `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/service/grpc_timeout.rs` and `channel/mod.rs` layer `tokio::time::Sleep`-based timeouts on top of hyper's client (`hyper::client::conn::Builder`, `hyper::client::connect::HttpConnector`), so any change to hyper's `tokio::time` usage in connect/ping paths affects tonic's timeout composition.\n- **`tokio::sync::{oneshot, watch}`** — `/workspace/hyper/src/common/drain.rs` (graceful shutdown signalling used by `hyper::Server`), `/workspace/hyper/src/client/dispatch.rs`, `/workspace/hyper/src/upgrade.rs`.\n  - **tonic usage:** `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/mod.rs` calls `hyper::Server::builder(incoming)` (line ~498) and relies on hyper's drain/shutdown machinery for tonic's own graceful-shutdown support — an indirect dependency on `tokio::sync::watch` inside hyper.\n- **`tokio::spawn` / `tokio::task::JoinHandle`** — `/workspace/hyper/src/common/exec.rs` (default executor), used whenever tonic's `Server` runs without a custom executor.\n- **`tokio::io::DuplexStream`** — used directly by tonic (not through hyper) in `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/channel/mod.rs` for in-process/mock channels (`Endpoint::connect_with_connector` style tests), a separate direct tokio dependency layered alongside the hyper-mediated one.\n\n**Conclusion:** hyper is not a clean abstraction boundary for tokio in this version pair. tonic's public transport API (`Connected`, `ServerIo`, `BoxedIo`, `Server::serve_with_incoming`) is generically bounded on `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite}` and, on the server-default path, concretely typed on `hyper::server::conn::AddrStream` which is itself a thin wrapper over `tokio::net::TcpStream`. Any breaking change to `tokio::io::AsyncRead`/`AsyncWrite` trait signatures, `tokio::net::TcpStream`, or `tokio::time::Sleep`/`sleep`/`timeout` propagates through hyper into tonic's public API, not just its internals.\n\n## 3. Version Pinning Conflicts\n\n1. **hyper floor mismatch:** tonic 0.6.0 (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml`) requires `hyper = \"0.14.4\"`, but the hyper checkout in this workspace is `v0.14.0` (`/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml`, `version = \"0.14.0\"`). Building tonic against this exact hyper checkout via `path` overrides would work locally (path deps bypass semver resolution), but publishing/consuming tonic 0.6.0 from crates.io against a real dependency graph would reject any hyper `<0.14.4` — meaning bug/security fixes landing between 0.14.0 and 0.14.4 in hyper are load-bearing for tonic and this checkout is behind them.\n2. **tokio floor mismatch (tonic vs hyper):** tonic's transport feature requires `tokio = \"1.0.1\"` while hyper only requires `tokio = \"1\"` (effectively `>=1.0.0, <2.0.0`). This is not a hard conflict (Cargo unifies to the higher floor, 1.0.1, since both are compatible under the same `^1` semver range), but it means tonic implicitly assumes a tokio patch fix present in 1.0.1 that is not guaranteed by hyper's own declared constraint — if hyper's constraint were ever tightened independently, or if a tool resolves hyper's requirement in isolation, 1.0.0 could be selected and fail to satisfy tonic.\n3. **h2 duplicated constraint, independently versioned:** both `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml` (`h2 = { version = \"0.3\", optional = true }`) and `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml` (`h2 = {version = \"0.3\", optional = true}`) declare direct dependencies on `h2 = \"0.3\"`. tonic uses `h2` directly (for HTTP/2-level errors/reason codes in its transport error handling) while also getting it transitively through hyper's `http2` feature. Since both ranges are `^0.3`, Cargo will unify to one resolved version, but this is a case where tonic reaches around hyper to depend on hyper's own transport dependency directly — an upgrade of `h2` needs to satisfy both hyper's and tonic's constraints simultaneously, and any h2 API tonic uses directly that hyper's declared `0.3` range doesn't guarantee is a latent break risk.\n4. **tower version skew across the graph:** tonic's transport feature depends on `tower = \"0.4.7\"` with a curated feature subset (`balance, buffer, discover, limit, load, make, timeout, util`), while `tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml` dev-dependencies and `/workspace/tonic/examples/Cargo.toml` pull `tower = \"0.4\"` / `{version = \"0.4.7\", features = [\"full\"]}`. Not a conflict per se (same `^0.4.7` range) but any tower upgrade must be validated against the narrower feature set tonic actually ships with in production (`transport` feature), not just the `full`-featured dev/examples build.\n5. **No TLS-layer conflict currently, but a coordination risk:** tonic's `tls` feature adds `tokio-rustls = \"0.22\"` (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml`), which itself depends on a specific tokio range. hyper does not depend on tokio-rustls at all — TLS is entirely tonic's own dependency edge, layered on top of hyper's plain-TCP `AddrStream`/`HttpConnector`. A tokio major-version bump therefore has **two independent propagation paths into tonic**: through hyper (tokio ^1, feature-gated) and through tokio-rustls (tokio ^1, separately gated by the `tls` feature) — both must be bumped in lockstep or tonic's `tls` feature alone can desync from its `transport` feature.\n\n## 4. Upgrade Coordination Strategy\n\nA tokio version bump must be coordinated bottom-up through this stack:\n\n1. **Bump tokio first, in isolation.** Land the tokio version bump and confirm `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite, ReadBuf}`, `tokio::net::{TcpListener, TcpStream}`, `tokio::time::{Sleep, sleep, timeout}`, and `tokio::sync::{oneshot, watch}` retain their current signatures — these are the exact symbols hyper re-exports/wraps (Section 2). Any signature change here is a breaking change for hyper even if hyper's own code doesn't change.\n2. **Bump hyper's `tokio` dependency and re-verify hyper's `full` feature build.** Because hyper 0.14 has no I/O-runtime abstraction layer, a tokio `AsyncRead`/`AsyncWrite` trait change requires editing `/workspace/hyper/src/server/tcp.rs` (`AddrStream`'s trait impls), `/workspace/hyper/src/common/io/rewind.rs`, `/workspace/hyper/src/proto/h1/io.rs`, and `/workspace/hyper/src/proto/h2/{client,server}.rs` directly. Release a new hyper patch/minor version once this is validated.\n3. **Bump the hyper floor in tonic's `Cargo.toml`** (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml`, currently `hyper = \"0.14.4\"`) to the new hyper version, and separately confirm tonic's own direct tokio usages remain valid:\n   - `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/conn.rs` (`tokio::net::TcpStream`, `hyper::server::conn::AddrStream`)\n   - `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/incoming.rs` (`AsyncRead + AsyncWrite` bound on `tcp_incoming`)\n   - `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/service/io.rs` (`Io` trait / `BoxedIo`)\n   - `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/channel/mod.rs` (`tokio::io::DuplexStream`, `hyper::client::connect::Connection`)\n   These are the exact places where a tokio trait/type change surfaces as a compile break in tonic, independent of whether hyper's public API changed.\n4. **Bump `tokio-rustls` for the `tls` feature in lockstep**, since it is a second, independent tokio-version-sensitive edge not mediated by hyper at all (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml`, `tokio-rustls = {version = \"0.22\", optional = true}`). Validate `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/service/tls.rs` separately from the plain-TCP path.\n5. **Validate feature unification**, not just per-crate builds: build tonic with `default-features` (`transport, codegen, prost`) *and* with `tls` enabled, since tokio feature flags (`sync, net, rt, time, macros`) are unioned across hyper's `full` feature and tonic's own explicit `tokio/macros`/`tokio/time` requests (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml` `transport = [..., \"tokio/macros\", \"tokio/time\"]`). A tokio release that removes or feature-gates one of these differently would need the union re-checked.\n6. **Run tonic's own integration/interop suites last** (`/workspace/tonic/tests/integration_tests`, `/workspace/tonic/interop`, `/workspace/tonic/tonic-web/tests/integration`) — these exercise the real hyper `Server`/`Client` + tokio TCP/TLS paths end-to-end and are the only checks that would catch a behavioral (not just signature) change, e.g. in `tokio::time` timeout semantics or `tokio::net::TcpListener` accept-loop backoff behavior (`/workspace/hyper/src/server/tcp.rs` lines ~100–170).\n\n**Priority order:** tokio → hyper → tonic (+ tokio-rustls in parallel with the hyper step, gated on the `tls` feature) → tonic-health/tonic-reflection/tonic-web (leaf crates, lower risk — they depend on tokio only for `sync`/`net` features, not the deep I/O coupling described above).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56089,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f8170ca-8e65-4dbe-b7f8-5bbd0b3c22fc","uuid":"ccb4156f-b2ca-40af-b167-6efdbb93fdaf","timestamp":"2026-07-29T12:00:14.910Z","request_id":"req_011CdWJxWcXYwhFnMEN83Qh6"}
